{
  "what": "Which tasks a calendar day shows, in which order, with which time and which marker — and how the backlog rail cuts its weeks. A table of inputs and the answers shared/taskDay.ts gives for each.",
  "why": "These rules are asked on both surfaces while rendering (the day, week and month views, the mobile day list, the backlog rail). They are moving into cal-core, where a Rust implementation has to give the same answers; while both exist this file is what keeps them together, and once the TypeScript goes it is the record of what the rules did on the day they moved. Written by running the TypeScript BEFORE the port.",
  "writtenBy": [
    "src/intl/taskDay.measure.test.ts — a one-off, run once and deleted; its tables mirror src/intl/taskDay.test.ts and src/state/backlogWeeks.test.ts plus the rows the port needs that those never had (the ownership filter, the two-level scale, several days in one ask, a completion day on a list that hides completed tasks, an end time, a Saturday week)."
  ],
  "readBy": [
    "src/intl/taskDay.contract.test.ts",
    "crates/cal-core/src/task_day.rs (once the port exists)"
  ],
  "whereItLives": {
    "note": "Inside cal-core, like taskGrouping.json: twelve adapter repositories compile cal-core, and an include_str! reaching out of the crate would break the day it moves."
  },
  "notInThisTable": {
    "todayIsoKey": "reads the clock; stays on the calling side, which passes the day in",
    "mergeDayItems": "sorts task times against event times the caller gives as epoch milliseconds, composed through the local Date — a rendering step, pinned by src/intl/taskDay.test.ts",
    "localTimeZone": "the LOCAL day of completed_at is resolved by the caller (localDateKey, the device zone) and handed over as completed_day; the core reads no zone. The late-evening case lives in src/intl/taskDay.test.ts, where the machine zone is the point."
  },
  "shape": {
    "language": "the app language tag the answers were measured under (the ordering within a day collates titles)",
    "baseTask": "the Task every onDay case starts from; a case’s `tasks` entries are overrides merged over it",
    "onDay": {
      "input": {
        "tasks": "overrides over baseTask; a completed task also carries `completed_day`, the local day of `completed_at` as the shell resolves it (noon UTC instants here, so every zone agrees)",
        "days": "the days asked about, YYYY-MM-DD",
        "completedVisible": "list ids whose completed tasks are shown (the per-list opt-in); absent means none",
        "currentUserByList": "list id → the connected user, for the ownership filter; absent means no gating; null means a list with no identity, which keeps everything",
        "scale": "\"three\" (default) or \"two\""
      },
      "expect": "day → rows in display order: {id, time, endTime, deadlineChip}"
    },
    "weeks": "{today, weekStartsOn (0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday)} → {thisWeekStart, thisWeekEnd, nextWeekStart, nextWeekEnd}, inclusive day keys",
    "deadlineSplit": "{deadlines: [{id, deadline_date}], weeks} → {thisWeek, nextWeek, later} as ids in input order; an overdue deadline goes with this week"
  },
  "language": "de",
  "baseTask": {
